Torchlight @VERSION@ for Linux

Install it for yourself (no root needed):

    ./install.sh

This puts the programs in ~/.local/bin and starts the search daemon, now and at
each login. Then bind a keyboard shortcut, such as Super+Space, to:

    ~/.local/bin/torchlight-gtk --toggle

To update, run install.sh from a newer release. To remove Torchlight, run
./install.sh --uninstall (your index and settings stay unless you delete them).

It needs a 64-bit PC with GTK 4.14 or newer and glibc 2.39 or newer: Fedora 40,
Debian 13, Ubuntu 24.04, openSUSE Tumbleweed, Arch and others from 2024 on.

https://github.com/antash-mishra/torchlight
